BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lunch & Learn: The Charleston Patriots: Strangers in a Strange Lan
 d
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T133000
UID:10003172-1794916800-1794922200@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2026/08/Ryals-11.17-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lunch and Learns
DESCRIPTION:A few months after the surrender of Charles Town in 1780 the B
 ritish rounded up and arrested sixty-three of the most prominent leaders o
 f the Revolutionary movement in South Carolina despite pledging on their h
 onor that they would not violate the terms of their parole. They were sent
  to East Florida where they were held against their will under town arrest
  in St. Augustine as prisoners of war for 9 months. \nRobert Ryals returns
  to the Rev War Visitor Center to share this dramatic and sometimes amusin
 g historic storytelling experience based on the diary and experiences of J
 osiah Smith\, a Charles Town merchant. \nRSVP @ simplyrevolutionary.com \n
 You bring your lunch and we will provide the learning opportunity!
LOCATION:Revolutionary War Visitor Center\, 212 Broad Street\, Camden\, SC
 \, 29020\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/lunch-learn-the-charleston-patriots
 -strangers-in-a-strange-land/
END:VEVENT
