DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261118T190000
UID:10003235-1795024800-1795028400@southcarolina250.com
CATEGORIES:Events,Lectures
DESCRIPTION:A lecture by historian and battlefield preservationist Durant 
 Ashmore. At the first Siege of Ninety Six (November 19–21\, 1775)\, Jame
 s Birmingham was killed\, the first South Carolinian to die in the name of
  Liberty. Durant discusses the events that led to his death.
LOCATION:Captain Kimberly Hampton Library\, 304 Biltmore Rd\, Easley\, SC\
 , 29640\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/first-blood-the-first-siege-of-nine
 ty-six/
